# RR2c-2a (critical_qualifier_receivers_bug; steps/qualifier-receivers-20261010.md; the author, 2026-10-10,
# LMX_blog/2026-10-10.md#qualifier-receivers-20261010: three receivers consuming any Structure): the qualifier chain
# over a merge in a declaration's tail, in a method -- `a: independent: const: immutable: merge(Integer  int: value
# 7)` -- is the author's chain over a value made at run time: the result is built under its own profile, proved and
# sealed before publication, its root free of a lexical parent; its fields read as any merge result's; a later merge
# over it retains it by its profile (docs #composition) and reads through.  `const` alone and `independent` alone are
# their own contracts over the same merge.  Exit 7; 81..85 name the failing read.
Integer:
    int: value 0
end: Integer
Extra:
    int: more 2
end: Extra
fn: m () int
    a: independent: const: immutable: merge(Integer  int: value 7)
    if: a\value != 7
        return: 81
    b: independent: const: immutable: merge(Integer; (int: value 9))
    if: b\value != 9
        return: 82
    c: merge(a; Extra)
    if: c\value * 10 + c\more != 72
        return: 83
    d: const: merge(Integer  int: value 3)
    if: d\value != 3
        return: 84
    e: independent: merge(Integer  int: value 4)
    if: e\value != 4
        return: 85
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
